import{_ as a,o as t,c as r,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.uPk2SrVb.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-03 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence","description":"Execution admission, cancellation/recovery, log security and cross-device delivery; 16 groups with precise merge/release states.","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-03 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence","description":"Execution admission, cancellation/recovery, log security and cross-device delivery; 16 groups with precise merge/release states."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-03.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-03.md","lastUpdated":null}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-03.md"};function s(o,e,l,c,d,p){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="_2026-11-03-agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-03 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-03-agent-research-and-competitor-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-03 Agent Research and Competitor Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The main development is that <strong>governance is becoming concrete contracts for execution admission, captured call permissions, cancellation cleanup, durable evidence and recovery ownership.</strong> Changes across Codex, ADK, LangGraph, OpenHands and Paperclip reinforce this direction. Orca and Agentlas have stable releases; AG2 event trees remain under review. A merge is not a stable release or production qualification.</p><p>Actual execution began <strong>2026-11-03 10:03:00 Asia/Shanghai (02:03:00 UTC)</strong>. The normal incremental window begins at the previous start, 2026-11-02 02:46:49 UTC; commit queries use retained per-source successful baselines. The latest-main Registry still contains <strong>47 researchers</strong>. Repositories are evidence sources, not grounds to attribute contributor changes as a researcher&#39;s new paper. Yue Zhao is recorded as <strong>赵越</strong> in Chinese.</p><h2 id="_1-codex-host-admission-and-captured-mcp-permissions" tabindex="-1">1. Codex: host admission and captured MCP permissions <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-codex-host-admission-and-captured-mcp-permissions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Codex: host admission and captured MCP permissions&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#58963 #59020 #59028 MERGED; stable release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Host ownership adds a turn-admission provider, including for root turns, and keeps its execution guard for the task lifetime. Admission waits remain interruptible and accept input; failures enter the turn lifecycle. Prepared MCP calls retain both permissions and the working/home/temp directories and workspace roots that interpret them. Guardian uses that captured context for denied-path evidence across runtime refreshes. Sandbox context stays out of serialized approval actions.</p><p>This separates execution capacity, task ownership and call-permission evidence. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: whether admission leases span actual execution and review uses the same captured permission context.</p><p>Worth discussing: how do cancellation during admission and permission refresh prove guards and review context cannot leak across turns?</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/58963" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#58963</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/59020" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#59020</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/59028" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#59028</a></p><h2 id="_2-claude-code-2-1-317-fail-closed-hooks-persistence-failures-and-session-isolation" tabindex="-1">2. Claude Code 2.1.317: fail-closed hooks, persistence failures and session isolation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-claude-code-2-1-317-fail-closed-hooks-persistence-failures-and-session-isolation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Claude Code 2.1.317: fail-closed hooks, persistence failures and session isolation&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：v2.1.317 RELEASED (stable)</strong></p><p>Agent SDK hook callbacks gain onFailure: block; unexpected connectors on a new cloud schedule trigger a warning. Nested claude -p in cloud/self-hosted runners no longer shares the outer session ID and transcript or resumes the wrong conversation after restart; self-hosted users have a compatibility switch. Lost transcript/config writes on full disks or quota now produce exit 1 in text/json modes, although full NFS exports may be missed. Restart while awaiting plan approval also preserves conversation state.</p><p>A successful exit is not persistence proof. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: hook failure defaults, nested-session identity and terminal states for failed persistence.</p><p>Worth discussing: NFS detection limits and transcript isolation with the compatibility switch enabled.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.317" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v2.1.317</a></p><h2 id="_3-google-adk-cancellation-teardown-sqlite-serialization-and-skill-yaml-boundaries" tabindex="-1">3. Google ADK: cancellation teardown, SQLite serialization and Skill/YAML boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-google-adk-cancellation-teardown-sqlite-serialization-and-skill-yaml-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. Google ADK: cancellation teardown, SQLite serialization and Skill/YAML boundaries&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：7 commits on default branch; #7652 MERGED via commit; stable release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>A2A cancel signals the active Runner, awaits cleanup and classifies INVOCATION_ABORTED as CANCELED. Shared teardown seals dangling ordinary tool calls, while paused long-running calls remain unsealed. Both SQLite session services use BEGIN IMMEDIATE across stale checks, state merges and writes. Skill execution removes free-form command in favor of validated paths and structured arguments. YAML loading blocks private toggles and executable entry points and applies the denylist to legacy from_config. Missing rubric verdicts become unscored; invocation-level rubric matching remains a limitation.</p><p>These address canceled-but-running tools, lost concurrent state, configuration becoming execution authority, and scoring without evidence. All CodeFlowMu/FCoP relevance remains pending local validation.</p><p>Worth discussing: proof that side effects stop before cancel returns, long-running-call exceptions and rubric alignment across invocations.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/bc0b41871699a70a3bf1169bb7e7ff91d2db5e31" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">bc0b418716</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/c3abc93d11260e87bb1bd1445faa25a6b5b0d681" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">c3abc93d11</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/ff61524bb1378bd355d92b5b88955ea142f83be0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ff61524bb1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/d1f2add4fe759c7c9109cba5eae2b20809fc6795" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">d1f2add4fe</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/1c7e8f76b6c995b69b5cc9ec1ac2960988388a1d" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">1c7e8f76b6</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/14765ab2bf78500e167ccd08c97cffd9b143a80d" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">14765ab2bf</a> · <a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/abd8f0f69bab8d5ee9b3e0e5a88d42b57e69b3d6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">abd8f0f69b</a></p><h2 id="_4-langgraph-python-sdk-clean-stream-closure-is-not-run-completion" tabindex="-1">4. LangGraph Python SDK: clean stream closure is not run completion <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-langgraph-python-sdk-clean-stream-closure-is-not-run-completion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4. LangGraph Python SDK: clean stream closure is not run completion&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#9554 MERGED; release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>After a clean close without end/error, the SDK checks run status when Location names a thread-scoped run stream. Pending/running or transient check failures use the existing reconnect budget, backoff and cursor. Terminal status and cases such as non-429 4xx keep the ending behavior. Thread streams, missing Location and legacy threadless Locations are unchanged. The cost is an extra GET that may download a large run input again.</p><p>This prevents proxy timeouts or restarts from silently truncating answers as success. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: separate connection termination from task completion and account for reconnect cost.</p><p>Worth discussing: can a lightweight terminal-state endpoint avoid fetching input again while preserving cursor idempotence?</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/9554" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9554</a></p><h2 id="_5-openhands-sdk-encryption-at-rest-for-bash-event-logs" tabindex="-1">5. OpenHands SDK: encryption at rest for bash event logs <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-openhands-sdk-encryption-at-rest-for-bash-event-logs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5. OpenHands SDK: encryption at rest for bash event logs&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#6343 MERGED; general stable rollout NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>The public PR describes a disclosure involving bash logs exposed with a sandbox file tree; command/output logs can contain credentials. With a configured cipher, BashEventService writes Fernet tokens and reads with previous keys. Undecryptable files are logged and skipped. Legacy plaintext remains readable without automatic re-encryption, and no secret key still means plaintext writes. Deployment fixes moving state off published trees and uploading secrets belong to other repositories; this does not prove every deployment safe. A real sandbox was not tested in the PR.</p><p>The boundary includes logs, volumes and recovery archives. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: protection with/without keys, rotation and legacy backups.</p><p>Worth discussing: legacy plaintext migration/deletion and whether unreadable events become explicit audit gaps.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6343" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#6343</a></p><h2 id="_6-langfuse-bounded-capture-memory-and-explicit-mcp-tool-failures" tabindex="-1">6. Langfuse: bounded capture memory and explicit MCP tool failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-langfuse-bounded-capture-memory-and-explicit-mcp-tool-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;6. Langfuse: bounded capture memory and explicit MCP tool failures&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#19576 #19579 MERGED; release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Gateway keeps raw JSON instead of expanding a 5 MiB request into a 128–483 MiB Value tree. An upstream standalone counting allocator measured about 5 MiB on the new path; this is not our local test. Parsed configuration/metadata share a 64 KiB budget; excess fields stay in input, preserving raw JSON formatting. Upstream response parsing is outside scope. MCP handler failures become isError: true tool results, carrying approved-call failures into the agent conversation rather than only throwing protocol errors.</p><p>Audit capture must respect resource admission and preserve tool failures. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: capture budgets and failure visibility in recovery/evaluation.</p><p>Worth discussing: balancing raw JSON, bounded field parsing, retrieval and privacy.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/19576" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#19576</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/19579" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#19579</a></p><h2 id="_7-github-mcp-server-experimental-issue-artifact-tools-merged" tabindex="-1">7. GitHub MCP Server: experimental issue-artifact tools merged <a class="header-anchor" href="#_7-github-mcp-server-experimental-issue-artifact-tools-merged" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;7. GitHub MCP Server: experimental issue-artifact tools merged&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#3554 MERGED; experimental opt-in; release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>New issue_artifact_read (list/get) and issue_artifact_write (create/update/delete) store plans, instructions and references on issues. issue_artifacts requires opt-in, even in Insiders; read-only exposes only reads. Operations use issue-scoped artifact_number, and enabling tools grants no API permission. Lockdown rejects operations because responses lack authors for trust checks; writes are not automatically retried. Author testing covers one repository/credential lifecycle, not all hosts.</p><p>This adds structured task evidence while exposing an author-identity trust gap. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: evidence identity, authorization and retry policy.</p><p>Worth discussing: is an auditable restricted-read mode possible without author metadata?</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server/pull/3554" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#3554</a></p><h2 id="_8-paperclip-lost-acquire-replies-restart-stop-cleanup-and-workspace-writers" tabindex="-1">8. Paperclip: lost acquire replies, restart Stop cleanup and workspace writers <a class="header-anchor" href="#_8-paperclip-lost-acquire-replies-restart-stop-cleanup-and-workspace-writers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;8. Paperclip: lost acquire replies, restart Stop cleanup and workspace writers&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#18692 #18682 #18691 MERGED; stable release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Opted-in providers can recover a lost-acquire resource identity from the creation journal, but identity is not termination proof: exact stop receipts remain required to release ownership. After restart, exactly bound pending Stop/audit, recovery lease/generation and the original budget reservation allow cleanup of the existing session without a new paid turn; missing usage retains debt. Children inheriting an actively written workspace use scheduled retry; stale or stopped-but-unsaved writers still need reconciliation. Controlled PostgreSQL/IPC and CI evidence is not production VM/hosted-credential qualification.</p><p>Learning high; competitive risk high. Radar: recovery and ownership implementation improves, but production recovery is not qualified. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: distinguish identity, termination receipt, cancellation ACK and billing settlement.</p><p>Worth discussing: retaining uncertainty after binding/credential loss and proving cleanup cannot submit a new turn.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/18692" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#18692</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/18682" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#18682</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/18691" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#18691</a></p><h2 id="_9-beads-configuration-authority-argv-injection-and-local-proxy-authentication" tabindex="-1">9. Beads: configuration authority, argv injection and local proxy authentication <a class="header-anchor" href="#_9-beads-configuration-authority-argv-injection-and-local-proxy-authentication" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;9. Beads: configuration authority, argv injection and local proxy authentication&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#7879 #7881 #7885 MERGED; release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Repository .beads/.env no longer imports executable credential-runner/editor/pager settings. mail.delegate trusts only process environment and user-global config; workspace API writes are rejected. Sync remotes starting with - are refused, and MCP argv uses -- and --flag=value so text cannot become options. Loopback data connections require an HMAC token derived from an owner-only secret; control probes use nonce/HMAC instead of sending the secret. Dolt launches from a validated private config snapshot; CA checks include primary-group sharing. Mixed-version proxies are incompatible and must be stopped on upgrade.</p><p>Learning high; competitive risk medium-high. Radar: stronger security with real upgrade costs. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: repository data versus user authority, local multi-user isolation and validation-to-use consistency.</p><p>Worth discussing: remaining boundaries of ready-line checks and private snapshots on platforms such as Windows.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/7879" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#7879</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/7881" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#7881</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/pull/7885" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#7885</a></p><h2 id="_10-orca-1-4-246-orchestrator-v3-and-mobile-operations-released" tabindex="-1">10. Orca 1.4.246: Orchestrator V3 and mobile operations released <a class="header-anchor" href="#_10-orca-1-4-246-orchestrator-v3-and-mobile-operations-released" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;10. Orca 1.4.246: Orchestrator V3 and mobile operations released&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：v1.4.246 RELEASED (stable)</strong></p><p>Release notes introduce Orchestrator V3 for CLI agents and Chat UI and filter worker notifications during orchestration. Chat UI leaves experimental, with queued follow-ups, steering and continuation through another account/harness after usage limits. Mobile can run automations and handle merge conflicts/PR operations; browser/computer use and terminal restores also change. Token-efficiency/reliability improvements are release claims, without an independent benchmark in this run.</p><p>Learning high; competitive risk high. Radar: stronger released delivery and mobile control; performance advantage remains unquantified. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: task/evidence controls on mobile and identity/authority across account/harness continuation.</p><p>Worth discussing: revalidating tool permissions, credential boundaries and side-effect ownership when switching accounts.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/releases/tag/v1.4.246" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.4.246</a></p><h2 id="_11-agentlas-os-standalone-engine-channel-and-host-environment-isolation" tabindex="-1">11. Agentlas OS: standalone engine channel and host environment isolation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_11-agentlas-os-standalone-engine-channel-and-host-environment-isolation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;11. Agentlas OS: standalone engine channel and host environment isolation&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：os-v1.2.73 / os-v1.2.74 RELEASED (stable standalone channel); legacy latest unchanged</strong></p><p>The standalone engine installs in ~/.agentlas/os-runtime with an os-bin launcher and leaves Desktop runtime intact. Optional memory/index/auto-update/telemetry features default off; graph automation and Telegram/Connect commands leave the engine without deleting data. 1.2.74 prevents host sessions from leaking engine-locator variables into Claude/Codex, where another older plugin could replace the standalone runtime. Antigravity registration is explicit. Existing v1.2.72 installs do not automatically switch channels.</p><p>Learning medium-high; competitive risk medium. Radar: watch standalone-engine delivery boundaries; reliability is not independently validated. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: install channels, host plugins and engine-locator environment isolation.</p><p>Worth discussing: resolution order and diagnostics for multiple host/plugin/engine versions.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/agentlas-ai/Agentlas-OS/releases/tag/os-v1.2.73" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">os-v1.2.73</a> · <a href="https://github.com/agentlas-ai/Agentlas-OS/releases/tag/os-v1.2.74" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">os-v1.2.74</a></p><h2 id="_12-orkas-preserve-evidence-on-invalid-transcription-and-failed-writes" tabindex="-1">12. Orkas: preserve evidence on invalid transcription and failed writes <a class="header-anchor" href="#_12-orkas-preserve-evidence-on-invalid-transcription-and-failed-writes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;12. Orkas: preserve evidence on invalid transcription and failed writes&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#161 MERGED; release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Native Whisper output is validated before replacing a usable transcript, with valid replacements published through the atomic JSON writer. Invalid output is a recoverable tool error; interrupted writes preserve the old transcript and source media. Valid silence, explicit retry and workspace confinement remain. Upstream reports 231 deterministic cases and three Electron journeys, using controlled ASR executables, without live transcription-quality or physical Windows qualification.</p><p>Learning medium-high; competitive risk medium. Radar: stronger evidence preservation/recovery; Windows delivery and live quality remain unqualified. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: retries must not destroy the last usable result.</p><p>Worth discussing: distinguishing retryable output from irreplaceable source evidence after atomic-publish failure.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/161" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#161</a></p><h2 id="_13-eigent-event-timeline-becomes-default-with-build-time-rollback" tabindex="-1">13. Eigent: event timeline becomes default with build-time rollback <a class="header-anchor" href="#_13-eigent-event-timeline-becomes-default-with-build-time-rollback" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;13. Eigent: event timeline becomes default with build-time rollback&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#2114 MERGED after v1.0.7; next release inclusion NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Normal builds enable the event-native timeline with inline approvals, task narrative and model switches. VITE_CHATBOX_EVENT_BUS=false restores the old view only through a new build; historical sessions without timeline events still fall back. Upstream reports 992 cases for default/rollback paths and discloses baseline failures. In-app human verification is not complete; the legacy renderer remains for at least two to three releases.</p><p>Learning medium-high; competitive risk medium. Radar: governance events become default interaction, with delivery/manual-QA gaps retained. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: event-derived approval/state projections and evidenced historical compatibility/rollback.</p><p>Worth discussing: which governance facts can be reconstructed for event-less legacy sessions, and which must stay unknown?</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/eigent-ai/eigent/pull/2114" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#2114</a></p><h2 id="_14-paradev-formerly-superset-attachment-delivery-sleeping-workspaces-and-missed-schedules" tabindex="-1">14. Paradev (formerly Superset): attachment delivery, sleeping workspaces and missed schedules <a class="header-anchor" href="#_14-paradev-formerly-superset-attachment-delivery-sleeping-workspaces-and-missed-schedules" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;14. Paradev (formerly Superset): attachment delivery, sleeping workspaces and missed schedules&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#9064 #9257 #9274 #9270 MERGED; release/deployed behavior NOT VERIFIED</strong></p><p>Attachments route by local/remote/cloud placement through local copy, remote transfer or fileId storage. Large local files can be paths; relay limits are 25 MB. Integrated desktop/mobile/recreated-box manual testing is owed, and durable event-log/shared-view pieces remain missing. CLI metadata management of sleeping cloud workspaces avoids waking sandboxes; restart/unarchive/real-teammate sharing lack production tests. Sorting numeric RRULE BYHOUR/BYMINUTE/BYSECOND repairs midnight-wrap and unordered-slot skips. Upstream read-only inspection found four affected triggers; post-merge deployment behavior is unverified. Chat fixes approval waits, background holds and compaction steering; SUPER-2700 still lacks a confirmed root cause.</p><p>Learning high; competitive risk high. Radar: stronger cross-device workspaces/scheduling without treating merges or unit tests as full production acceptance. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: attachment location/identity, control plane independent of runtime, and independent expected-slot checks.</p><p>Worth discussing: independently detecting slots a schedule library never emits, and proving durable attachment delivery across devices.</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9064" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9064</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9257" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9257</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9274" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9274</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9270" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#9270</a></p><h2 id="_15-ag2-subagent-event-trees-and-scoped-variables-remain-under-review" tabindex="-1">15. AG2: subagent event trees and scoped variables remain under review <a class="header-anchor" href="#_15-ag2-subagent-event-trees-and-scoped-variables-remain-under-review" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;15. AG2: subagent event trees and scoped variables remain under review&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：#3526 #3523 #3524 OPEN (not draft); NOT MERGED / NOT RELEASED</strong></p><p>#3526 head changed at 21:20 UTC on November 2, preserving original usage/task lifecycle event types with provenance and excluding custom inert events from conversation history. The proposal lets ancestors observe descendant events, reply to a concrete invocation and cancel its descendants; operational ChildEvent observations do not execute ancestor tools/HITL. Scoped bindings stay within one invocation tree; fresh roots copy caller inputs. Layer tests are reported passing, but review approval is still required. This is a current integration revision of an older proposal, not a release.</p><p>Relevant to subagent observability, accounting attribution and cross-user isolation. Pending CodeFlowMu/FCoP validation: observation must not grant execution authority, and storage/compaction must retain original spender/invocation identity.</p><p>Worth discussing: can one invocation-provenance model verify ancestor visibility, targeted cancellation and shared-binding boundaries?</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/pull/3526" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#3526</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/pull/3523" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#3523</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/pull/3524" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#3524</a></p><h2 id="_16-copilot-cli-prerelease-fixes-credential-echo-hooks-and-background-delivery" tabindex="-1">16. Copilot CLI: prerelease fixes credential echo, hooks and background delivery <a class="header-anchor" href="#_16-copilot-cli-prerelease-fixes-credential-echo-hooks-and-background-delivery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;16. Copilot CLI: prerelease fixes credential echo, hooks and background delivery&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Status：v1.0.106-3 / -4 / -5 RELEASED (prerelease); not stable</strong></p><p>The latest prerelease stops invalid-header BYOK keys from appearing in errors/session logs, ignores empty hook-modified prompts with a field warning, and explicitly fails MCP enable when repository policy disables the server. Background completions arriving after autopilot stops are delivered with the next user message. Two earlier prereleases in this window harden terminal control-character escaping, hook depth and permission/session-recovery errors. These are prerelease capabilities only.</p><p>Relevant to credential isolation, hook contracts and reliable asynchronous delivery. CodeFlowMu/FCoP relevance is pending validation; release notes do not establish the same local defects.</p><p>Worth discussing: retaining original task/session identity for delayed delivery without cross-turn misattribution?</p><p><strong>Primary public sources：</strong> <a href="https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/releases/tag/v1.0.106-5" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.0.106-5</a> · <a href="https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/releases/tag/v1.0.106-4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.0.106-4</a> · <a href="https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/releases/tag/v1.0.106-3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">v1.0.106-3</a></p><h2 id="cross-project-patterns-and-classification" tabindex="-1">Cross-project patterns and classification <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-project-patterns-and-classification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-project patterns and classification&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Pre-action governance:</strong> Codex host admission/MCP snapshots, ADK Skill/YAML constraints and Beads user-level executable configuration distinguish observing configuration from execution authority.</li><li><strong>Completion and recovery semantics:</strong> ADK cancellation, LangGraph run queries, Paperclip exact Stop/receipts and Paradev input-wait states separate connection, task, background work and cleanup terminal states.</li><li><strong>Evidence and resource boundaries:</strong> OpenHands encryption, Langfuse bounded capture, Orkas atomic replacement and AG2 provenance require recoverable facts plus explicit gaps and costs.</li><li><strong>Delivery and mobile:</strong> Orca mobile operations, location-aware Paradev attachments and Agentlas standalone engines separate control and execution planes without proving cross-device security or production reliability.</li></ul><p>This run is information gathering and classification: <strong>16 information groups; 0 local research experiments, 0 experiment articles, 0 formal development reviews and 0 external comments</strong>. Upstream tests/performance numbers are upstream evidence, not our experiments. Every CodeFlowMu/FCoP link remains a validation lead, with no development assignment or Research Runtime lifecycle changes. Technical discussion angles are recorded; no comments were sent.</p><h2 id="dual-source-checks-deduplication-and-coverage-gaps" tabindex="-1">Dual-source checks, deduplication and coverage gaps <a class="header-anchor" href="#dual-source-checks-deduplication-and-coverage-gaps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dual-source checks, deduplication and coverage gaps&quot;">​</a></h2><p>GitHub checks covered commit queries, the latest 5 updated Issue/PR records and latest 3 releases for 88 target repositories, retaining 500 commits (including canonical Paradev follow-up), 174 Issue/PR records and 189 release records. These are inspected records, not new findings or research outputs. Orca commits stop at the first 100 and remain incomplete; TSA is inaccessible. The old Superset path redirects; 30 commits were checked at the previously verified Paradev canonical repository without changing radar identity. Full 5-item Issue/PR and 3-item release pages are partial coverage and do not advance full-history baselines. An interrupted 30-item list batch is not counted successful; all 88 targets were subsequently rechecked with a 5-item bound. Older pending windows remain; unknown is not no-change.</p><p>The separate public-web source class checked <a href="https://cursor.com/changelog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cursor changelog</a>, <a href="https://cursor.com/docs/release-notes/cloud-agents" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloud Agents release notes</a>, <a href="https://auditable-agents.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Auditable Agents</a>, <a href="https://auditcommons.org/latest/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Audit Commons latest</a> and targeted Yue Zhao searches. Accessible pages did not verify a newly dated technical publication in this run; October 25/27 material and upcoming talks are not presented as today&#39;s news. The USC profile returned 502; another unverified address failed and was not used for identity. This is not exhaustive coverage of all 47 researchers&#39; X replies/threads, Roadmaps/Discussions, READMEs, licenses or security advisories. Source classes are kept separate; primary GitHub engineering evidence independently supports the reported facts.</p><p>No new checked commits were found in Zhao&#39;s specified repositories or the six governance subjects&#39; repositories. MAST, AgentSpec, manifests, steganography and failure attribution retain their distinct relationships. bulbasaur-skill-cli remains a related project, <strong>not the official AGENTSAFE artifact</strong>. Registry repository paths are preserved without substituting authors/implementations based on similar names.</p><p>Existing daily reports were used for deduplication. MCP #3471/#3452 have recent updated_at values, but inspected text, closures and comments are old and excluded from new findings. Only AG2&#39;s current head integration revision is reported as new. Historical gaps and pagination debt remain in local coverage/checkpoints.</p><h2 id="archive-and-website-publication" tabindex="-1">Archive and website publication <a class="header-anchor" href="#archive-and-website-publication" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Archive and website publication&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Only this report, its Chinese mirror and the two date indexes are source-write targets, committed with GitHub app tooling. The existing VitePress pages, fixed entries and public snapshots are preserved. After source submission, a build and non-force gh-pages publication must be followed by matching Pages-run verification and unique-first live bilingual indexes plus full reports. Final acceptance is recorded in this run&#39;s chat and local publication receipt; source existence alone is not website delivery.</p>',109)])])}const g=a(i,[["render",s]]);export{h as __pageData,g as default};
